# PROJECT: ENGLISH PRO – Personal English & Civil Engineering Coach

## 1. ROLE AND PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior Android software architect, professional English language-learning specialist, applied linguist, AI conversation designer, speech-processing engineer, and educational UX designer.

Build a complete, production-quality native Android application called **English Pro**.

The application is a personalized English-learning system designed for an adult learner who previously had an Upper-Intermediate (B2) English level and an IELTS Academic/General equivalent score of approximately 6.0, but has not actively practiced English for several years.

The learner has lost some vocabulary recall, speaking fluency, listening confidence, and spontaneous communication ability.

The primary objectives are:

1. Restore and significantly improve spontaneous English speaking ability.
2. Expand active vocabulary and improve long-term vocabulary retention.
3. Improve listening comprehension and pronunciation.
4. Develop natural, fluent everyday conversational English.
5. Develop professional English for working in an international civil engineering and construction company.
6. Prepare the learner to participate confidently in technical meetings, construction site discussions, progress meetings, coordination meetings, negotiations, and professional communications.
7. Make the application highly functional offline, without requiring an internet connection for its essential learning features.

Do not treat this learner as a beginner.

Start with a comprehensive placement assessment and dynamically determine the actual current level. Use CEFR levels A2, B1, B2, C1 and their sublevels where appropriate.

The target is strong B2 moving toward C1, with particular emphasis on speaking and professional communication.

Do not teach basic English unnecessarily unless the assessment identifies a specific weakness.

