# 6. OFFLINE-FIRST ARCHITECTURE

Offline operation is a fundamental requirement, not an optional feature.

The application must remain useful when the phone has no internet connection for several weeks or months.

Implement a local-first architecture.

### Offline features that must work

- Vocabulary browsing.
- Vocabulary learning.
- Flashcards.
- Spaced repetition.
- Search.
- Persian translations.
- Grammar lessons.
- Downloaded listening exercises.
- Downloaded audio pronunciation.
- Recorded speaking practice.
- Previously downloaded role-play scenarios.
- Scenario-based conversation with predefined branching responses.
- Local speech recognition where a compatible model is installed.
- Local text-to-speech where an offline voice is available.
- Progress tracking.
- Statistics.
- Local backup and restore.

Do not make the app dependent on Gemini API availability.

### Online-only enhancements

When internet is available, provide:

- Advanced AI conversation.
- Dynamic role-play generation.
- Detailed grammar correction.
- Advanced speaking analysis.
- Generation of new vocabulary exercises.
- Generation of personalized lessons.
- Downloading new content packages.
- Synchronization and backup if enabled by the learner.

When the connection is lost, switch automatically to offline mode.

Never show a blank screen or disable the entire learning module because an API is unavailable.

Clearly indicate whether the user is in online or offline mode.

### Local database

Use Room Database with SQLite.

Store:

- Vocabulary.
- Learning progress.
- Review schedules.
- Conversation history.
- Speaking recordings.
- Transcriptions.
- User settings.
- Downloaded lessons.
- Learning statistics.

All essential learning records must persist after closing and restarting the application.

Use database migrations to protect existing user data when the app is updated.

### Data backup

Provide:

- Export of personal learning data.
- Import and restore.
- JSON or another documented portable format.
- Backup of vocabulary and learning progress.
- Optional inclusion of recordings.

Do not require an account or cloud connection for the basic application.

